# Build output
/binnacle
/sextant
/dist/

# Test and coverage artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# Local plan and working notes: they name real clusters and real people.
/docs/plan.md
/docs/consolidation-plan.md
/docs/consolidation-flaws.md
/docs/management-cluster.md
/docs/sextant-refactor.md
/docs/master-plan.md
/docs/notes/

# Local tooling
/bin/
/.claude/

# Site overlays: real hostnames, real registries, real namespaces. The tracked
# manifests in deploy/ stay generic; what actually gets applied does not.
/deploy/sites/

# Screenshots taken against a live fleet carry hostnames, IP pools and
# inventory. Nothing rendered from a real cluster belongs in the tree.
#
# Anchored to the repo root rather than matching every PNG anywhere: a
# screenshot gets dropped where you happen to be standing, while brand artwork
# and the marks built from it live in assets/ and internal/web/static/ and are
# tracked on purpose.
/*.png
/*.jpg

# Anything holding credentials
*.kubeconfig
clouds.yaml
.env

# Editor and OS files belong in your global gitignore, not here:
#   git config --global core.excludesfile ~/.gitignore
